<Project>

  <Import Project="$([MSBuild]::GetPathOfFileAbove('Directory.Build.props', '$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../'))" />

  <!--
    TestBed is the fixture, and its defects are the specification.

    It contains, on purpose: a god object, a concealed decision hidden in plumbing, seven
    near-identical normalizers with one planted outlier, a DIP contrast pair, a namespace
    cycle between TestBed.Core and TestBed.Core.Pricing, two projects nothing references,
    a type named like data access that is not, and scaffolded code that must be excluded.

    Every assertion in tests/Bearing.Tests is a claim about this exact shape — 51 types,
    131 edges, 8 cohorts, 2 excluded. Tidying it up, enabling nullable, or letting an
    analyzer talk anyone into a "harmless" refactor changes the expected answers and
    breaks the suite for reasons that have nothing to do with Bearing.

    Treat this directory as data. If you need a new case, ADD to it — do not reshape what
    is here, and update the known answers in docs/TESTING.md when you do.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>false</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <EnableNETAnalyzers>false</EnableNETAnalyzers>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>false</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    <AnalysisLevel>none</AnalysisLevel>
    <WarningLevel>0</WarningLevel>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS0169;CS0414;CS0649;CS8618</NoWarn>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
